mo_ta_cong_viec:
MoMo is looking for a DevSecOps Engineer who builds CI/CD pipelines while embedding security into every step of that pipeline. This role suits someone with a solid DevOps foundation who also has deep security knowledge in application/infrastructure security.
Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines (GitLab CI preferred), focusing on Infrastructure as Code, reliability, and traceability;
Automate deployment strategies: blue-green, canary, rolling;
Integrate security into the pipeline: SAST, DAST, SCA, secret scanning, image scanning;
Assess and remediate security risks (blue team approach), investigate and handle security incidents;
Support migration of services from monolith to microservices on Kubernetes, hybrid-cloud environment;
Ensure proper security configuration on cloud platforms (AWS/Azure/GCP);
Build monitoring/alerting systems with Prometheus/Grafana.

yeu_cau:
2–4 years of experience, with a solid foundation in both CI/CD and Security;
Proven experience integrating security tooling into real production pipelines;
Experience proactively proposing/deciding on security solutions;
Understanding of cloud platforms (AWS/Azure/GCP) from a security perspective;
Proficient in Python, Bash (Go/Java is a plus);
CCNA certification or equivalent networking certification required;
Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or a related field.
